[Function.prototype.bind](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Function/bind) doesn't modify the original `finish` function, so that line has no effect as is. You would need to do something like:

```js
const finishWithIndex = finish.bind({ index: i });

// ... and below, change occurrences of `finish` in the function scope
destroys.push(destroyer(ret, false, true, finishWithIndex));
```

